      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok I conflated this timeout with event processing when they are mostly not related. This check is checking that when the gate merges code the expected ref shows up in the code base afterwards. That will emit events that we process but we\u0027re processing things mostly independently of one another.\n\nThat should mean there isn\u0027t a case where we enter this method while we\u0027re already past the timeout and never check if the ref is present in the first place. This was my primary concern hence the suggestion that we maybe check at least once if the timeout is hit. But I think we\u0027re already doing that so all is well.",
